  <running_head>GEORGII HORNII</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">Ducatus Gelriæ &amp; Comitatus Zutpha-</l>
    <l n="2">niæ Ordines, Hardervicense Gymna-</l>
    <l n="3">sium, jure &amp; privilegiis Academiæ do-</l>
    <l n="4">narunt. Verba huc spectantia hæc sunt:</l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Concessimus &amp; indulsimus, &amp; Diplomate</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>hoc concedimus atque indulgemus, ut Il-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>lustris hoc Tetrarchia Velavica Gymna-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>sium bonis avibus ad Provincialis Aca-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>demia fastigium ascendat, &amp; eandem au-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>ctoritatem, idem jus ac privilegia obtineat,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>quibus ab conditoribus suis Vniversitates</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>alia ornata atque adsecta sunt. Ea pro-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>pter advocatis Academia nova clarissimis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Professoribus, ac vocandis deinceps, pote-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>statem facimus, præcedente justo examine,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>&amp; spectata Candidatorum peritia, crean-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>di facultatum omnium Doctores, Licen-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>tiatos, ac Magistros,dandique indices eru-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>ditionis &amp; honoris tabulas, quas dignita-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>tis ejusdem atque æstimationis haberi</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>volumus, cujus sunt, quæ ab Academiis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>reliquis &amp; Vniversitatibus conceduntur.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">Ex quibus manifestissimum est, Acade-</l>
    <l n="24">miam hanc, æque magna obtinere privi-</l>
    <l n="25">legia &amp; authoritatem, ac aliæ quævis,sive</l>
    <l n="26">à Pont. Romano, sive Cæsare, Regibus,</l>
    <l n="27">Principibus, ac Rebuspubl. constitutæ</l>
    <l n="28">Academiæ. Cum enim Ordines fœderati</l>
    <l n="29">Belgiĭn universum, ac separatim singu-</l>
    <l n="30">larum Provinciarum,nullum in his terris</l>
    <l n="31">Domi-</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The line "Belgiĭn" shows a stray mark over the i; I have read it as Belgii. Words broken at line ends keep their printed hyphen. The running head is set in small capitals and is given as printed.</notes>
